00:18:10,497 --> 00:18:11,849
These aren't surprises,

577
00:18:11,849 --> 00:18:13,202
they're just irregular.

578
00:18:13,382 --> 00:18:15,628
Set aside a small amount each month

579
00:18:15,628 --> 00:18:18,258
for each one in separate savings buckets.

580
00:18:18,438 --> 00:18:19,638
When the bill arrives,

581
00:18:19,638 --> 00:18:20,783
the money is waiting.

582
00:18:21,134 --> 00:18:22,065
To set one up,

583
00:18:22,065 --> 00:18:24,859
list your irregular expenses for the year,

584
00:18:24,859 --> 00:18:25,657
add them up,

585
00:18:25,657 --> 00:18:27,055
and divide by twelve.

586
00:18:27,235 --> 00:18:29,384
If they total twenty four hundred dollars,

587
00:18:29,384 --> 00:18:30,869
you need two hundred a month.

588
00:18:31,049 --> 00:18:33,750
Many banks let you create several savings

589
00:18:33,750 --> 00:18:36,122
buckets inside one account for free.

590
00:18:36,472 --> 00:18:37,412
Move nineteen.

591
00:18:37,592 --> 00:18:38,393
Talk about money.

592
00:18:38,743 --> 00:18:41,438
If you're in a serious relationship,

593
00:18:41,438 --> 00:18:43,160
talk about money early:

594
00:18:43,160 --> 00:18:45,407
debts, goals, spending styles.

595
00:18:45,587 --> 00:18:47,986
Money conflicts are a common source of

596
00:18:47,986 --> 00:18:49,186
stress for couples.

597
00:18:49,366 --> 00:18:51,443
And find at least one friend who's

598
00:18:51,443 --> 00:18:53,336
also working on their finances.

599
00:18:53,516 --> 00:18:54,643
Good habits spread.

600
00:18:54,993 --> 00:18:56,894
And if your family never talked about

601
00:18:56,894 --> 00:18:58,127
money, you're not alone.

602
00:18:58,307 --> 00:19:00,304
Many people learn as adults.

603
00:19:00,484 --> 00:19:03,397
Books, podcasts and free resources from the

604
00:19:03,397 --> 00:19:06,717
Consumer Financial Protection Bureau can fill the

605
00:19:06,717 --> 00:19:07,055
gaps.

606
00:19:07,235 --> 00:19:09,300
Curiosity about money is one of the

607
00:19:09,300 --> 00:19:10,835
best habits you can build.

608
00:19:11,185 --> 00:19:12,171
Move twenty.

609
00:19:12,351 --> 00:19:13,559
Review once a quarter.

610
00:19:13,909 --> 00:19:15,284
Every three months,

611
00:19:15,284 --> 00:19:18,469
spend fifteen minutes checking your savings,

612
00:19:18,469 --> 00:19:21,002
debts, net worth and contributions.

613
00:19:21,182 --> 00:19:24,169
Raise your retirement contribution by one percent

614
00:19:24,169 --> 00:19:24,839
if you can.

615
00:19:25,019 --> 00:19:26,940
These small check ins keep you on

616
00:19:26,940 --> 00:19:29,791
course without obsessing over daily market moves.

617
00:19:30,141 --> 00:19:31,017
Once a year,

618
00:19:31,017 --> 00:19:32,405
do a bigger review.

619
00:19:32,585 --> 00:19:33,933
Check your insurance,

620
00:19:33,933 --> 00:19:37,015
your beneficiaries, your credit reports and your

621
00:19:37,015 --> 00:19:37,914
overall goals.

622
00:19:38,094 --> 00:19:40,144
Write down your net worth and compare

623
00:19:40,144 --> 00:19:41,031
it to last year.

624
00:19:41,211 --> 00:19:42,936
Watching that number grow,

625
00:19:42,936 --> 00:19:44,992
even slowly, is one of the best

626
00:19:44,992 --> 00:19:46,319
motivators there is.

627
00:19:46,670 --> 00:19:48,797
Twenty moves can feel like a lot,

628
00:19:48,797 --> 00:19:50,408
so here's a simple order.

629
00:19:50,588 --> 00:19:52,794
First year: moves one through five.

630
00:19:52,974 --> 00:19:54,095
Track your money,

631
00:19:54,095 --> 00:19:55,811
open a high yield account,

632
00:19:55,811 --> 00:19:57,592
build one thousand dollars,

633
00:19:57,592 --> 00:20:00,033
automate it, and take the full match.

634
00:20:00,213 --> 00:20:01,768
These are the foundations.

635
00:20:02,119 --> 00:20:03,490
Years two and three:

636
00:20:03,490 --> 00:20:04,998
moves six through ten.

637
00:20:05,178 --> 00:20:06,369
Open a Roth IRA,

638
00:20:06,369 --> 00:20:07,858
choose simple funds,

639
00:20:07,858 --> 00:20:09,794
attack high interest debt,

640
00:20:09,794 --> 00:20:11,655
make a student loan plan,

641
00:20:11,655 --> 00:20:13,293
and build your credit.

642
00:20:13,473 --> 00:20:15,016
This is when you go from not

643
00:20:15,016 --> 00:20:16,945
losing ground to actually building.

644
00:20:17,295 --> 00:20:19,010
And throughout your twenties:

645
00:20:19,010 --> 00:20:20,371
moves eleven to twenty.

646
00:20:20,551 --> 00:20:23,137
Keep your car and housing reasonable,

647
00:20:23,137 --> 00:20:24,116
learn to cook,

648
00:20:24,116 --> 00:20:26,353
protect yourself with insurance,

649
00:20:26,353 --> 00:20:27,541
invest in skills,

650
00:20:27,541 --> 00:20:29,917
negotiate pay, use the raise rule,

651
00:20:29,917 --> 00:20:31,385
set up sinking funds,

652
00:20:31,385 --> 00:20:32,573
talk about money,

653
00:20:32,573 --> 00:20:34,321
and review every quarter.

654
00:20:34,501 --> 00:20:36,522
These are the habits that carry the

655
00:20:36,522 --> 00:20:36,811
plan.

656
00:20:37,161 --> 00:20:38,983
Year one: foundations.

657
00:20:39,163 --> 00:20:40,729
Years two and three:

658
00:20:40,729 --> 00:20:41,903
start building.

659
00:20:42,083 --> 00:20:44,548
All decade: the habits that carry the

660
00:20:44,548 --> 00:20:44,881
plan.

661
00:20:45,232 --> 00:20:47,729
So what does a good financial twenties

662
00:20:47,729 --> 00:20:49,109
look like by the end?

663
00:20:49,289 --> 00:20:51,919
Here's a realistic target many people can

664
00:20:51,919 --> 00:20:53,330
work toward by thirty.

665
00:20:53,510 --> 00:20:55,977
Three to six months of expenses in

666
00:20:55,977 --> 00:20:57,283
an emergency fund.

667
00:20:57,463 --> 00:20:58,821
No credit card debt.

668
00:20:59,001 --> 00:21:01,068
A plan for student loans.

669
00:21:01,248 --> 00:21:02,699
A good credit score.

670
00:21:02,879 --> 00:21:05,605
And retirement savings equal to about one

671
00:21:05,605 --> 00:21:06,934
year of your salary,

672
00:21:06,934 --> 00:21:09,328
a rough benchmark used by firms like

673
00:21:09,328 --> 00:21:09,926
Fidelity.

674
00:21:10,277 --> 00:21:11,818
If you don't hit all of those

675
00:21:11,818 --> 00:21:13,040
by thirty, that's okay.

676
00:21:13,220 --> 00:21:15,228
They're guidelines, not a test.

677
00:21:15,408 --> 00:21:17,883
Someone who starts at twenty seven with

678
00:21:17,883 --> 00:21:20,295
student loans may be behind on savings

679
00:21:20,295 --> 00:21:21,945
but making great progress.

680
00:21:22,125 --> 00:21:24,502
What matters most is that the machine

681
00:21:24,502 --> 00:21:25,851
is built and running.

682
00:21:26,202 --> 00:21:27,780
Let's meet three people.

683
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:30,399
Jordan earns forty two thousand dollars at

684
00:21:30,399 --> 00:21:31,153
twenty three.

685
00:21:31,333 --> 00:21:33,144
He lives with two roommates,

686
00:21:33,144 --> 00:21:34,825
drives a ten year old car,

687
00:21:34,825 --> 00:21:36,184
takes the full match,

688
00:21:36,184 --> 00:21:38,059
and opens a Roth IRA with one

689
00:21:38,059 --> 00:21:39,611
hundred dollars a month.

690
00:21:39,791 --> 00:21:41,254
It doesn't feel like much.

691
00:21:41,434 --> 00:21:43,466
He sometimes wonders if it's worth it.

692
00:21:43,816 --> 00:21:46,344
Priya earns fifty five thousand dollars at

693
00:21:46,344 --> 00:21:47,066
twenty four.

694
00:21:47,246 --> 00:21:48,961
She buys a new car with a

695
00:21:48,961 --> 00:21:50,812
six hundred dollar payment,

696
00:21:50,812 --> 00:21:53,143
moves into a nice apartment alone,

697
00:21:53,143 --> 00:21:55,269
and puts trips on credit cards.

698
00:21:55,449 --> 00:21:56,912
She's having fun.

699
00:21:57,092 --> 00:21:59,472
She plans to get serious at thirty.

700
00:21:59,822 --> 00:22:02,651
And Marcus earns thirty eight thousand dollars

701
00:22:02,651 --> 00:22:05,111
at twenty five with twenty five thousand

702
00:22:05,111 --> 00:22:06,648
dollars in student loans.

703
00:22:06,828 --> 00:22:08,404
He builds a starter fund,

704
00:22:08,404 --> 00:22:09,854
signs up for the match,

705
00:22:09,854 --> 00:22:12,628
and takes a weekend certification that bumps

706
00:22:12,628 --> 00:22:13,132
his pay.

707
00:22:13,312 --> 00:22:15,321
He uses the raise rule every year.

708
00:22:15,671 --> 00:22:18,643
By thirty, Jordan has a growing portfolio

709
00:22:18,643 --> 00:22:20,818
and no debt beyond a small car

710
00:22:20,818 --> 00:22:22,486
loan he paid off early.

711
00:22:22,666 --> 00:22:25,529
Marcus has cleared his highest rate loans,

712
00:22:25,529 --> 00:22:27,029
earns noticeably more,

713
00:22:27,029 --> 00:22:29,074
and has a real emergency fund.

714
00:22:29,254 --> 00:22:31,744
Priya has a higher salary than both

715
00:22:31,744 --> 00:22:34,020
of them, but she has credit card

716
00:22:34,020 --> 00:22:36,225
debt, a car worth less than she

717
00:22:36,225 --> 00:22:38,217
owes, and almost no savings.

718
00:22:38,568 --> 00:22:40,390
Priya isn't a bad person.

719
00:22:40,570 --> 00:22:42,556
She did what felt normal.

720
00:22:42,736 --> 00:22:45,308
And she can absolutely turn things around

721
00:22:45,308 --> 00:22:46,311
in her thirties.

722
00:22:46,491 --> 00:22:48,439
But she'll be starting from behind,

723
00:22:48,439 --> 00:22:50,553
while Jordan and Marcus have a machine

724
00:22:50,553 --> 00:22:51,832
that's already running.

725
00:22:52,012 --> 00:22:54,357
That's the quiet power of your twenties.

726
00:22:54,708 --> 00:22:57,384
It's worth acknowledging that people in their

727
00:22:57,384 --> 00:22:59,526
twenties today face real challenges.

728
00:22:59,706 --> 00:23:02,351
Housing costs in many cities have risen

729
00:23:02,351 --> 00:23:03,572
faster than wages.

730
00:23:03,752 --> 00:23:05,990
Student debt is much higher than it

731
00:23:05,990 --> 00:23:07,780
was for earlier generations.

732
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:10,604
And many jobs no longer offer traditional

733
00:23:10,604 --> 00:23:14,601
pensions, which once provided retirement income automatically.

734
00:23:14,952 --> 00:23:17,204
But there are real advantages too.

735
00:23:17,384 --> 00:23:20,543
Earlier generations often paid high commissions to

736
00:23:20,543 --> 00:23:21,238
buy stocks.

737
00:23:21,418 --> 00:23:24,822
Today, many brokers offer commission free trades,

738
00:23:24,822 --> 00:23:27,044
and broad index funds can cost a

739
00:23:27,044 --> 00:23:29,406
tiny fraction of a percent a year.

740
00:23:29,586 --> 00:23:31,272
You can open an account from your

741
00:23:31,272 --> 00:23:32,140
phone in minutes.

742
00:23:32,320 --> 00:23:35,522
Automatic enrollment in workplace plans has become

743
00:23:35,522 --> 00:23:36,291
more common.

744
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:38,848
So the playing field has changed in

745
00:23:38,848 --> 00:23:39,856
both directions.

746
00:23:40,036 --> 00:23:42,382
Housing and education cost more.

747
00:23:42,562 --> 00:23:44,512
Investing costs much less.

748
00:23:44,692 --> 00:23:46,762
That's why the moves in this video

749
00:23:46,762 --> 00:23:48,954
focus on keeping big fixed costs low

750
00:23:48,954 --> 00:23:51,450
and getting your money invested early and

751
00:23:51,450 --> 00:23:51,937
cheaply.

752
00:23:52,117 --> 00:23:53,905
You can't control rent prices.

753
00:23:54,085 --> 00:23:56,178
You can control your savings rate and

754
00:23:56,178 --> 00:23:56,743
your fees.

755
00:23:57,094 --> 00:23:58,463
Let's make this concrete.

756
00:23:58,643 --> 00:24:00,549
Here's what to do with your very

757
00:24:00,549 --> 00:24:02,037
first full time paycheck,

758
00:24:02,037 --> 00:24:02,811
step by step.

759
00:24:03,161 --> 00:24:05,567
Say you earn forty five thousand dollars

760
00:24:05,567 --> 00:24:07,491
a year and you're paid every two

761
00:24:07,491 --> 00:24:07,852
weeks.

762
00:24:08,032 --> 00:24:10,364
Your gross pay is about seventeen hundred

763
00:24:10,364 --> 00:24:11,956
thirty dollars per paycheck.

764
00:24:12,136 --> 00:24:14,413
After federal and state taxes,

765
00:24:14,413 --> 00:24:16,387
Social Security, Medicare,

766
00:24:16,387 --> 00:24:19,424
health insurance and a five percent 401k

767
00:24:19,424 --> 00:24:22,536
contribution, your take home pay might be

768
00:24:22,536 --> 00:24:24,965
around thirteen hundred dollars.

769
00:24:25,145 --> 00:24:27,807
Your exact number will depend on your

770
00:24:27,807 --> 00:24:29,174
state and benefits.

771
00:24:29,523 --> 00:24:31,664
Before that money hits your account,

772
00:24:31,664 --> 00:24:33,864
the five percent is already invested,

773
00:24:33,864 --> 00:24:35,766
and if your employer matches it,

774
00:24:35,766 --> 00:24:37,372
you're investing even more.

775
00:24:37,552 --> 00:24:39,423
That's the best part of the paycheck,

776
00:24:39,423 --> 00:24:41,142
and you didn't have to do anything

777
00:24:41,142 --> 00:24:42,254
after the first setup.

778
00:24:42,603 --> 00:24:44,080
When the paycheck arrives,

779
00:24:44,080 --> 00:24:46,578
an automatic transfer of one hundred dollars

780
00:24:46,578 --> 00:24:48,850
goes to your high yield savings account.

781
00:24:49,030 --> 00:24:51,059
Then your fixed bills come out:

782
00:24:51,059 --> 00:24:52,237
half of your rent,

783
00:24:52,237 --> 00:24:54,397
your phone, a share of utilities,

784
00:24:54,397 --> 00:24:55,903
a student loan payment.

785
00:24:56,083 --> 00:24:58,196
What's left covers groceries,

786
00:24:58,196 --> 00:25:01,110
transport and fun until the next payday.

787
00:25:01,460 --> 00:25:03,910
Two paychecks a month cover your regular

788
00:25:03,910 --> 00:25:04,339
budget.

789
00:25:04,519 --> 00:25:05,680
And here's a bonus.

790
00:25:05,860 --> 00:25:06,745
In most years,

791
00:25:06,745 --> 00:25:09,020
being paid every two weeks gives you

792
00:25:09,020 --> 00:25:10,347
twenty six paychecks,

793
00:25:10,347 --> 00:25:12,559
which means two months have a third

794
00:25:12,559 --> 00:25:13,128
paycheck.

795
00:25:13,308 --> 00:25:16,264
Many people send those extra paychecks straight

796
00:25:16,264 --> 00:25:18,277
to their emergency fund or debt.

797
00:25:18,457 --> 00:25:20,565
That's two bonus paychecks a year,

798
00:25:20,565 --> 00:25:21,557
without a raise.

799
00:25:21,906 --> 00:25:23,991
Your twenties are often the best time

800
00:25:23,991 --> 00:25:25,738
to experiment with side income.

801
00:25:25,918 --> 00:25:27,886
You may have more free time and

802
00:25:27,886 --> 00:25:30,109
energy, and fewer responsibilities.

803
00:25:30,289 --> 00:25:32,831
Tutoring, freelancing, pet sitting,

804
00:25:32,831 --> 00:25:34,647
delivery, selling crafts,

805
00:25:34,647 --> 00:25:37,479
or building a small online business can

806
00:25:37,479 --> 00:25:39,948
add a few hundred dollars a month.

807
00:25:40,299 --> 00:25:42,481
The key is where that money goes.

808
00:25:42,661 --> 00:25:45,336
If side income disappears into lifestyle,

809
00:25:45,336 --> 00:25:47,294
it doesn't change your future.

810
00:25:47,474 --> 00:25:49,984
If it goes to your emergency fund,

811
00:25:49,984 --> 00:25:51,755
your debt or a Roth IRA,

812
00:25:51,755 --> 00:25:53,822
it can speed up your plan by

813
00:25:53,822 --> 00:25:54,265
years.

814
00:25:54,445 --> 00:25:56,757
Three hundred dollars a month of side

815
00:25:56,757 --> 00:25:59,194
income, invested for ten years at seven

816
00:25:59,194 --> 00:26:01,568
percent, could grow to about fifty two

817
00:26:01,568 --> 00:26:02,630
thousand dollars.

818
00:26:02,980 --> 00:26:04,374
And remember taxes.

819
00:26:04,554 --> 00:26:06,774
Side income is usually taxable,

820
00:26:06,774 --> 00:26:08,779
and if you're self employed,

821
00:26:08,779 --> 00:26:11,286
you may owe self employment tax and

822
00:26:11,286 --> 00:26:14,294
need to make estimated quarterly payments.

823
00:26:14,474 --> 00:26:16,728
Set aside a portion of what you

824
00:26:16,728 --> 00:26:17,818
earn for taxes,

825
00:26:17,818 --> 00:26:20,290
and check the IRS guidance for gig

826
00:26:20,290 --> 00:26:20,872
workers.

827
00:26:21,221 --> 00:26:23,532
Money stress is common in your twenties.

828
00:26:23,712 --> 00:26:27,602
Surveys from the American Psychological Association have

829
00:26:27,602 --> 00:26:29,686
found that money is one of the

830
00:26:29,686 --> 00:26:32,881
most frequently reported sources of stress for

831
00:26:32,881 --> 00:26:35,799
adults, and younger adults often report it

832
00:26:35,799 --> 00:26:36,146
most.

833
00:26:36,326 --> 00:26:38,112
If money keeps you up at night,

834
00:26:38,112 --> 00:26:39,380
you're far from alone.

835
00:26:39,729 --> 00:26:41,911
The good news is that small actions

836
00:26:41,911 --> 00:26:44,466
often reduce stress faster than big ones.

837
00:26:44,646 --> 00:26:47,234
Building the first five hundred dollars of

838
00:26:47,234 --> 00:26:49,699
savings, setting up autopay so you never

839
00:26:49,699 --> 00:26:50,439
miss a bill,

840
00:26:50,439 --> 00:26:52,472
or making a written plan for your

841
00:26:52,472 --> 00:26:54,444
debts can create a real sense of

842
00:26:54,444 --> 00:26:57,464
control, long before the numbers look impressive.

843
00:26:57,813 --> 00:26:59,679
And be kind to yourself about the

844
00:26:59,679 --> 00:26:59,961
past.

845
00:27:00,141 --> 00:27:02,066
Maybe you ran up a credit card

846
00:27:02,066 --> 00:27:04,376
in college or spent your first bonus

847
00:27:04,376 --> 00:27:05,018
on a trip.

848
00:27:05,198 --> 00:27:05,848
That's done.

849
00:27:06,028 --> 00:27:07,932
What matters is the next paycheck.

850
00:27:08,112 --> 00:27:10,382
Your twenties give you time to recover

851
00:27:10,382 --> 00:27:12,175
from almost any money mistake,

852
00:27:12,175 --> 00:27:14,207
as long as you start building now.

853
00:27:14,556 --> 00:27:16,491
If you're watching this near the end

854
00:27:16,491 --> 00:27:18,371
of your twenties with little saved,

855
00:27:18,371 --> 00:27:19,177
don't tune out.

856
00:27:19,357 --> 00:27:21,393
You still have more than thirty five

857
00:27:21,393 --> 00:27:23,711
years until a traditional retirement age.

858
00:27:23,891 --> 00:27:26,295
Two hundred fifty dollars a month from

